nside-the-rubble-like-a-miracle-three-days-after-indonesia-earthquake/articleshow/133375466.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/84-year-old-woman-found-alive-inside-the-rubble-like-a-miracle-three-days-after-indonesia-earthquake/articleshow/133375466.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-20T21:20:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133377509,imgsize-1445568.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Help us: 4 Indian-origin teens from New Jersey call 911 during Mount Lafayette hike; they will have to pay a hefty fine for 'unprepared' adventure]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133381798.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/help-us-4-indian-origin-teens-from-new-jersey-call-911-during-mount-lafayette-hike-they-will-have-to-pay-a-hefty-fine-for-unprepared-adventure/articleshow/133381798.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/help-us-4-indian-origin-teens-from-new-jersey-call-911-during-mount-lafayette-hike-they-will-have-to-pay-a-hefty-fine-for-unprepared-adventure/articleshow/133381798.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-20T20:52:27+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133381840,imgsize-76534.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Separated by Hamas in Oct 7 attack, Israeli couple reunites to marry 10 months after engagement]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133380578.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/separated-by-hamas-in-oct-7-attack-israeli-couple-reunites-to-marry-10-months-after-engagement/articleshow/133380578.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/middle-east/separated-by-hamas-in-oct-7-attack-israeli-couple-reunites-to-marry-10-months-after-engagement/articleshow/133380578.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-20T20:43:01+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133381625,imgsize-56872.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Why Pakistan’s donkeys are becoming valuable in China: What is driving this surprising demand]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133381085.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Pakistani donkeys are increasingly valuable due to rising Chinese demand for ejiao.  China's own donkey population struggles to meet the demand for this traditional product.  Pakistan has become a key part of this international supply chain after finalizing export protocols.  The rising prices of donkeys impact local families who depend on them for livelihoods.  This situation highlights the complex intersection of local needs and global trade.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/why-pakistans-donkeys-are-becoming-valuable-in-china-what-is-driving-a-surprising-demand-for-the-humble-animal/articleshow/133381085.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/why-pakistans-donkeys-are-becoming-valuable-in-china-what-is-driving-a-surprising-demand-for-the-humble-animal/articleshow/133381085.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-20T20:27:35+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133381159,imgsize-1148815.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[She got her first dolls' house at 8; now, at 101, she runs a museum]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133380866.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Val Ripley, aged 101, continues her lifelong fascination with dolls' houses and their historical significance. Her childhood toy, lost during the war, was rediscovered and inspired a museum. This museum showcases miniature homes as documents of social history and changing lifestyles. The collection features dolls' houses dating back to 1840, reflecting evolving domestic life. Val's enduring connection to these tiny worlds spans nearly a century.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/in-1932-an-8-year-old-girl-was-gifted-her-first-dolls-house-for-christmas-then-came-world-war-2-now-the-101-year-old-woman-has-created-a-dolls-house-museum/articleshow/133380866.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/in-1932-an-8-year-old-girl-was-gifted-her-first-dolls-house-for-christmas-then-came-world-war-2-now-the-101-year-old-woman-has-created-a-dolls-house-museum/articleshow/133380866.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-20T20:14:03+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Lifestyle Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133380940,imgsize-1171212.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Car salesman becomes Belgian prince after DNA test confirms royal paternity]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133380602.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/car-salesman-becomes-belgian-prince-after-dna-test-confirms-royal-paternity/articleshow/133380602.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/car-salesman-becomes-belgian-prince-after-dna-test-confirms-royal-paternity/articleshow/133380602.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-20T20:04:23+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Prisha Patnaik</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133380833,imgsize-64160.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Texas woman left 6 acres in 1916; her governor son added 250 acres to create its first park]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133380780.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Isabella Neff's generous donation of six acres to the Leon River marked the beginning of Texas' first state park. Her son, Pat Neff, significantly augmented this by contributing an additional 250 acres. Developed by the Civilian Conservation Corps, the park faced challenges from flooding, necessitating ongoing repairs. Today, Mother Neff State Park is a shining example of familial generosity and commitment to preservation.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1916-a-texas-woman-left-six-acres-of-riverbank-for-the-public-her-governor-son-later-added-250-acres-and-the-tiny-gift-helped-create-texas-first-state-park/articleshow/133380780.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1916-a-texas-woman-left-six-acres-of-riverbank-for-the-public-her-governor-son-later-added-250-acres-and-the-tiny-gift-helped-create-texas-first-state-park/articleshow/133380780.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-20T20:07:17+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133380880,imgsize-2110064.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[US education department tells schools to stop ‘racial balancing’ in student discipline policies]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133380325.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/us-education-department-tells-schools-to-stop-racial-balancing-in-student-discipline-policies/articleshow/133380325.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/us-education-department-tells-schools-to-stop-racial-balancing-in-student-discipline-policies/articleshow/133380325.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-20T19:55:59+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133380654,imgsize-620776.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Massachusetts police officer accused of using Flock cameras to track her ex-girlfriend]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133378528.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a significant move, New Bedford police have paused their automated license plate reader system following allegations of misuse by officer Emily Pacheco. Investigations revealed a troubling number of searches for one specific vehicle's license plate. Pacheco is currently on administrative leave while inquiries continue, alongside an extended abuse prevention order from a judge. This incident raises critical issues regarding surveillance practices and the implications for data privacy.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/massachusetts-police-officer-accused-of-using-flock-cameras-to-track-her-ex-girlfriend-department-suspends-entire-system-after-her-plate-was-searched-a-concerning-number-of-times/articleshow/133378528.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/massachusetts-police-officer-accused-of-using-flock-cameras-to-track-her-ex-girlfriend-department-suspends-entire-system-after-her-plate-was-searched-a-concerning-number-of-times/articleshow/133378528.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-20T19:53:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133380564,imgsize-511542.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Estranged brother says Natalie Harp is delusionally obsessed with Donald Trump; President's son reacts]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133379490.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/estranged-brother-says-natalie-harp-is-delusionally-obsessed-with-donald-trump-presidents-son-reacts/articleshow/133379490.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/estranged-brother-says-natalie-harp-is-delusionally-obsessed-with-donald-trump-presidents-son-reacts/articleshow/133379490.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-20T19:19:31+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133379510,imgsize-38470.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[US Waffle House cook's rap praising chain topped 1 mn TikTok views; weeks later, he was fired]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133377282.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Edric Riley, known as “Rockstar Riley” and the “King of Waffle House”, went viral after his rap song “Waffy Options” praising the restaurant chain crossed 1 million TikTok views. Weeks later, Waffle House fired him, citing repeated violations of its rules on filming promotional content on company property. Riley says he was promoting a company he loved.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/atlanta-waffle-house-cooks-rap-praising-the-chain-topped-1-million-tiktok-views-weeks-later-he-says-he-was-fired-after-20-years-with-the-company/articleshow/133377282.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/atlanta-waffle-house-cooks-rap-praising-the-chain-topped-1-million-tiktok-views-weeks-later-he-says-he-was-fired-after-20-years-with-the-company/articleshow/133377282.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-20T21:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133378155,imgsize-68421.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Nathan Cofnas, who exposed Cambridge professor Jason Arday’s plagiarism, suspended by Ghent University]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133378918.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/nathan-cofnas-who-exposed-cambridge-professor-jason-ardays-plagiarism-suspended-by-ghent-university/articleshow/133378918.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/nathan-cofnas-who-exposed-cambridge-professor-jason-ardays-plagiarism-suspended-by-ghent-university/articleshow/133378918.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-20T18:50:28+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Gokul Ankari</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133379098,imgsize-731045.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[NASA offers up to $500,000 to develop technology for tracking atmospheric drag]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133378539.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In an effort to enhance the understanding of upper atmospheric conditi